> -I know from a spoiler, that my reward for solving sokoban, is a bag of 
> holding. However, I haven't identified it as such yet, but am already 
> using it. What is it's maximum capacity? Can it store even more, when 
> identified?

No. The capasity is infinite, but on the other hand you cannot put 
everything in it. It's weight is calculated based on the weight of the 
contents. From Dylan's spoiler tool-341.txt:

The weight of a bag of holding (wgt) -- including the 15 for the bag
itself -- depends on the weight of its contents (cwgt) and its blessed
status:
   blessed:   wgt = 15 + cwgt/4 + 1
   uncursed:  wgt = 15 + cwgt/2 + 1
   cursed:    wgt = 15 + cwgt*2

You may also lose items when you use a cursed bag of holding; each item
in the bag has a 1/13 chance of disappearing each time you apply or loot
the bag.

